mage": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/12"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/13"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/14"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/15"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/16"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/17"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "[18]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/18"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "9", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0009.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> is left to stand by the wall<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15680626333572435903\"><a href=\"#15680626333572435903\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans45\"><span id=\"documenttrans45\">45</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 1 Kings 16:11.</p><hr></div></div></aside> cursed are all those that shall lift up the heal<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3868320620594694024\"><a href=\"#3868320620594694024\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans46\"><span id=\"documenttrans46\">46</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 41:9; and John 13:18.</p><hr></div></div></aside> against mine anointed saith the Lord and cry they have sinned when they have not sined before me saith the Lord but have done that which was meat in mine eyes and which I <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12642233134662537620\"><a href=\"#12642233134662537620\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6221\" topic=\"x6221\" title=\"Commandment\">commanded</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commandment\"><p>Generally, a divine mandate that church members were expected to obey; more specifically, a text dictated by JS in the first-person voice of Deity that served to communicate knowledge and instruction to JS and his followers. Occasionally, other inspired texts...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/commandment\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> them but those who cry transgresion do it becaus they are the servants of sin<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15455360189805025430\"><a href=\"#15455360189805025430\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans47\"><span id=\"documenttrans47\">47</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See John 8:34; and Romans 6:17.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and are the children of disobediance<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11798239708451795456\"><a href=\"#11798239708451795456\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans48\"><span id=\"documenttrans48\">48</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Colossians 3:6; and Ephesians 2:2; 5:6.</p><hr></div></div></aside> themselvs and those who swear false against my servants that they might bring them unto bondage and death. Wo unto them because they have offended my little ones they shall be severed from the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4407104604822067891\"><a href=\"#4407104604822067891\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4097\" topic=\"x4097\" title=\"Ordinance\">ordinances</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Ordinance\"><p>A religious rite. JS taught that ordinances were covenants between man and God, in which believers could affirm faith, gain spiritual knowledge, and seek blessings. Some ordinances were considered requisite for salvation. The manner in which ordinances were...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/ordinance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> of mine house<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17387350082260623397\"><a href=\"#17387350082260623397\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans49\"><span id=\"documenttrans49\">49</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Ezekiel 43:11; 44:5; and Isaiah 56:7.</p><hr></div></div></aside> their basket shall not be full their houses and their barnes shall famish and they themselvs shall be dispised by those that flattered them they shall not have right to the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14118582722162825756\"><a href=\"#14118582722162825756\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4102\" topic=\"x4102\" title=\"Priesthood\">priesthood</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Priesthood\"><p>Power or authority of God. The priesthood was conferred through the laying on of hands upon adult male members of the church in good standing; no specialized training was required. Priesthood officers held responsibility for administering the sacrament of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/priesthood\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> nor their posterity after them from generation to generation it had been better for them that a millstone had been hanged about their necks and they drownd in the depth of the see<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5313374688946915907\"><a href=\"#5313374688946915907\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans50\"><span id=\"documenttrans50\">50</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 18:6; Mark 9:42; and Luke 17:2.</p><hr></div></div></aside> wo unto all those that discomfort my people and drive and murder and testify against them<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9618943922861446324\"><a href=\"#9618943922861446324\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans51\"><span id=\"documenttrans51\">51</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See, for example, information on the prosecution witnesses at the November 1838 hearing. (<a href=\"/intro/documents-volume-6-part-3-introduction-4-november-1838-16-april-1839\" class=\"article\">Introduction to Part 3: 4 Nov. 1838–16 Apr. 1839</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> saith the Lord of host a generation of viper<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3011469198026750692\"><a href=\"#3011469198026750692\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans52\"><span id=\"documenttrans52\">52</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 3:7; 12:34; 23:33; and Luke 3:7.</p><hr></div></div></aside> shall not escape the damnation of hell behold mine eye seeth and knoweth all their works<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7358350587011285050\"><a href=\"#7358350587011285050\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans53\"><span id=\"documenttrans53\">53</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 66:18; and Revelation 3:8, 15.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and I have in reserve a swift judgement in the season thereoff for them all for there is a time appointed to evry man [p. 9]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> is left to stand by the wall<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11354904536138033162\"><a href=\"#11354904536138033162\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans45\"><span id=\"documenttrans45\">45</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 1 Kings 16:11.</p><hr></div></div></aside> cursed are all those <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that shall lift up the heal<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14367249798159294832\"><a href=\"#14367249798159294832\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans46\"><span id=\"documenttrans46\">46</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 41:9; and John 13:18.</p><hr></div></div></aside> against mine anointed <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>saith the Lord and cry they have sin[n]ed when <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>they have not sined before me saith the Lord<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span> but have done that which was meat in mine <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>eyes and which I <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7026696367545545241\"><a href=\"#7026696367545545241\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6221\" topic=\"x6221\" title=\"Commandment\">commanded</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commandment\"><p>Generally, a divine mandate that church members were expected to obey; more specifically, a text dictated by JS in the first-person voice of Deity that served to communicate knowledge and instruction to JS and his followers. Occasionally, other inspired texts...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/commandment\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> them but those <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>who cry transgresion do it becaus they are <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the servants of sin<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13735992118364038591\"><a href=\"#13735992118364038591\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans47\"><span id=\"documenttrans47\">47</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See John 8:34; and Romans 6:17.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and are the children of disobedi<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ance<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17561308384272986018\"><a href=\"#17561308384272986018\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans48\"><span id=\"documenttrans48\">48</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Colossians 3:6; and Ephesians 2:2; 5:6.</p><hr></div></div></aside> themselvs and those who swear false <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>against my servants that they might bring <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>them unto bondage and death. Wo unto <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>them because they have offended my little ones <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>they shall be severed from the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1622266369344136972\"><a href=\"#1622266369344136972\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4097\" topic=\"x4097\" title=\"Ordinance\">ordinances</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Ordinance\"><p>A religious rite. JS taught that ordinances were covenants between man and God, in which believers could affirm faith, gain spiritual knowledge, and seek blessings. Some ordinances were considered requisite for salvation. The manner in which ordinances were...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/ordinance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> of mine <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>house<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14375452134101056860\"><a href=\"#14375452134101056860\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans49\"><span id=\"documenttrans49\">49</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Ezekiel 43:11; 44:5; and Isaiah 56:7.</p><hr></div></div></aside> their basket shall not be full their houses <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and their barnes shall famish and they themselvs <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall be dispised by those that flattered them <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>they shall not have right to the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1003319290978244130\"><a href=\"#1003319290978244130\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4102\" topic=\"x4102\" title=\"Priesthood\">priesthood</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Priesthood\"><p>Power or authority of God. The priesthood was conferred through the laying on of hands upon adult male members of the church in good standing; no specialized training was required. Priesthood officers held responsibility for administering the sacrament of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/priesthood\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> nor their <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>posterity after them from generation to generation <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>it had been better for them that a millstone had <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>been hanged about their necks and they <span class=\"deleted\">having</span> drownd <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>in the depth of the see<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7563161708670654575\"><a href=\"#7563161708670654575\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans50\"><span id=\"documenttrans50\">50</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 18:6; Mark 9:42; and Luke 17:2.</p><hr></div></div></aside> wo unto all those that <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>discomfort my people and drive and mur<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>der and testify against them<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1260036189517862958\"><a href=\"#1260036189517862958\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans51\"><span id=\"documenttrans51\">51</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See, for example, information on the prosecution witnesses at the November 1838 hearing. (<a href=\"/intro/documents-volume-6-part-3-introduction-4-november-1838-16-april-1839\" class=\"article\">Introduction to Part 3: 4 Nov. 1838–16 Apr. 1839</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> saith the Lord of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>host a generation of viper<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3310930156791892391\"><a href=\"#3310930156791892391\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans52\"><span id=\"documenttrans52\">52</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 3:7; 12:34; 23:33; and Luke 3:7.</p><hr></div></div></aside> shall not escape the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>damnation of hell behold mine eye<span class=\"deleted\">s</span> seeth and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>knoweth all their works<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"558514537969634173\"><a href=\"#558514537969634173\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans53\"><span id=\"documenttrans53\">53</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 66:18; and Revelation 3:8, 15.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and I have in reserve a <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>swift judgement in the season thereoff for them <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>all for there is a time appointed <span class=\"deleted\">for</span> &lt;​to​&gt; evry man [p. 9]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edwa